WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.733
Why do breaker tie rods break?

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:07.600
Tighten the nuts in the order the manual gives, crosswise and in stages.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:15.467
If the nuts are tightened unevenly, only some of the rods carry the load and the most loaded one breaks first.

4
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:23.700
Impact and vibration can loosen the nuts over time; a loose rod soon fatigues and the others carry its load.

5
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:31.067
Prying with the tool puts side loads on the body; the rods then carry bending as well as tension.

6
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:38.200
A break usually starts at the root of a thread or where the rod’s section changes, and comes without warning.
